    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1006">

                <pb facs="0914" n="810" xml:id="pg810"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.002/31.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-07-11T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1913—noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>318. Department’s July 10, 5 p.m.; my 315, July 8, 7 p.m. I understand perfectly
                    the limitations of the relations to maintain with this Government. The specific
                    instructions I desire are in the matter of attending the official reception of
                    the new Minister of Foreign Affairs or joining in such other manifestations
                    which accompany the installation of a new Minister. Absenting myself at this
                    time would be construed as an offensive act. The case was different when, in
                    company with the entire Diplomatic Corps, I attended the De la Barra reception,
                    as none of the Governments had then officially recognized this Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
